WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:01.890
Welcome back.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.220
Got your paints ready, easel set up

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.040
and all ready to do a fantastic painting with me?

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:06.560
Good.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.770
Tell you what, let's have them run all the colors

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.530
across the screen that you need to do this painting with me.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.310
And while they're doing that, let's go on up here

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.490
and let me tell you what I've already done.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.040
I've covered this canvas, which is an 18 by 24 as usual.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.860
I've covered it with a piece of contact paper

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.260
that has an oval cut in it.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.940
Now this is just normal old contact paper

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.220
you can pick up at your local hardware store,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.140
grocery store, whatever.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.980
I've just cut an oval out of it, stuck it on there.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.800
and then I've covered this whole inside

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.260
with liquid white as we normally do.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.610
Other than that, there's nothing different about that.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.600
I thought today we'd do a fantastic little winter scene

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.700
that I really think you're gonna enjoy.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.640
So tell you what, let's go on up here and get started,

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.530
and we'll take right off.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.150
I'm gonna start out today with a small amount

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:53.630
of Prussian blue, just a little bit,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.660
and a little touch of midnight black.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.590
So we have Prussian blue and midnight black, okay?

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.280
And just mix them right on the brush, like so.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.480
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.620
Now, using the little criss-cross, or X-strokes,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.650
let's just make a happy little sky.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.390
Now see how you're making these little X's?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.770
Just like so, start at the top and work downward.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.630
By starting at the top and working downward,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.100
your paint will mix with the liquid white

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:29.780
and automatically.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.720
Your sky will get lighter toward the horizon.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.740
And this is one of those little tricks

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.780
that helps create the illusion of depth and distance

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.420
in your painting.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:44.140
Still using the little criss-cross strokes, just like so.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.300
This is just Prussian blue and midnight black.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.240
Okay, and then while I have that color still on the brush,

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.400
maybe we'll have a little water in this.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.840
I love water, so I use the same colors.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.880
Just blue and black, or black and blue.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.390
Whatever you prefer.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.520
Okay, let's go right in here,

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.920
and I'll just go right across like so.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.760
I don't know exactly where the water's gonna be,

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.240
so anything that's not water, we'll make it snow.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.930
We'll make a little winter scene,

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.210
and all of this can be shadows,

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.950
so it really doesn't matter where you put this.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.110
Just have fun.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.800
Okay, now then, let's wash our brush.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:29.960
And we wash our brush with good old water.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.680
go odorless thinner, and be sure it's odorless.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.600
If it's not, son of a gun, you're gonna get run

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.980
right out of the house, you'll be working out in the yard.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:42.190
Shake off the excess, then just take out

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.050
all your hostilities.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.650
This is really where you have fun.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:46.630
Now then, with a good clean dry brush,

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.450
I'm gonna start in the light area and blend upward,

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:52.680
still using the little criss-cross strokes,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:59.980
little X-strokes, just blend upward, like so, like so.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.420
Okay, now, very lightly, we just go across

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.880
and take out all those brush strokes

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.480
so that it's pretty smooth.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.700
And if there's any areas that are real dark,

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.860
just blend them, and they'll blend right in.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.620
Liquid white underneath is fantastic,

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.450
and we'll take out all those dark areas.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.560
Now, I like to put a little black in this guy

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.200
since it's winter, I want to give the impression

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.900
that it's cold, and just go across this.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.180
just to smooth it out.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:36.640
Okay, and that quick we have a happy little sky.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.340
Now today, let's make some clouds up here.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.700
And for that, we'll use a one-inch brush.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.280
Now you can make these clouds with a one-inch brush,

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.960
two-inch brush, fan brush.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.520
Shoot, you can make them with your shoe.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.380
No big deal.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.880
Just take and pull this brush through the paint.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.260
Get a lot of paint on the brush.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.520
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:03:59.960
Now you have to make a big decision.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.260
Where does your cloud live?

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.940
I think, I think, yep, he lives right here.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.840
And making tiny little circles,

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:14.000
tiny little circles, continually, just like so, see?

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.490
Just happy little circles.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.750
Clouds, boy, they just float around and have a good time.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.980
And let your brush do that.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.020
There he is, maybe.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.300
Okay, let's have another one down here.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:29.980
Wherever you think.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.960
If you think a cloud lives,

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.140
that's exactly where that son of a gun lives.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:33.980
Just drop it in there.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:42.250
Okay, now I'm gonna take a clean, dry, two-inch brush

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.200
and use just the top of the brush

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.310
and very gently blend the bottom of the cloud out.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.780
Just blend the bottom of it out.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.910
We're not touching the top at all yet.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.350
Now then, we grab it and fluff it.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.280
Just fluff it up.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:04:59.980
And do the same.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.260
in circular strokes, avoid doing it straight up

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.560
or it looks like it's raining upward.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:04.880
That'll bother you.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:06.930
That'll really bother you.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.750
Same thing down here.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:11.950
Just blend it out, fluff it, fluff it, fluff it,

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.680
and go across.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.540
Now sometimes when you're painting clouds,

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.910
it's fun to do layers of clouds,

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:19.890
one on top of the other.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.170
So completely finish one and then come back

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:22.790
and watch here.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.900
See, we can go right in here

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.660
and drop in another happy little cloud

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.440
and maybe he lives right underneath here.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.630
It doesn't matter, wherever.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.460
You can put as many or as few clouds in your world as you want.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:42.010
Take our brush, give it a good little wrap,

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:43.820
and do the same thing.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:50.440
Just blend it out a little bit, and then pull it.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.190
Now this is two hairs and some air.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.550
In other words, it's extremely gentle.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.590
The paint that we use is very firm.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.560
So you can do all this blending

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.230
without becoming a mud mixer.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:07.650
If you use a very soft, slimy paint, you're in trouble.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.560
The only time we use soft paints is for highlights,

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.560
and normally that's yellow.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.250
Yellow is normally always a highlight color,

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.940
so that can be very soft, but these base colors,

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.200
you need to be strong, very, very strong.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:21.930
Tell you what let's do.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.160
Let's put some little trees back here in the background.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.550
I'll mix up some black.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.640
Some blue, I like that black and blue.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.170
And a little bit of Van Dyke Brown.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.160
Let me clean off my knife.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.650
And we'll take the round brush, and we're gonna tap.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:50.760
Just tap that right in there, like so, just like this.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.970
Now then, I want some background trees back in here.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:57.010
So all we're looking for right now is basic shapes.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:59.940
Start at the bottom of the tree and work upwards.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:09.100
So the bottom is darker than the top and put into some very basic shapes. I think I'll put a whole line across here

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.510
We'll just have trees all the way across

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:16.620
You know in the last series

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:25.120
I showed a little bird a little a little Robin that I was raising that that had lived with me since he was just a baby

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.980
And we've had so many people write tell us that they

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.310
but they've watched this and they wanna know

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.150
what happened to him.

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:33.550
Let me show you the robin.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.480
This little bird was orphaned and he lives with me now,

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.330
and I feed him every day and take care of him,

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.520
and pretty soon he's gonna be a big bird.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.990
He's gonna learn to fly, and we're gonna turn him loose

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.470
and send him back to nature.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:52.360
Now, just recently, myself and Diane Schaffer,

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.760
she's the bird lady here in Muncie,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.380
we released that robin when he was full grown.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.840
I had raised him from a little tiny baby.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:06.830
until he was a big bird, and Diane and I let him go close to her house, and that's really,

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:15.040
there he went. That really makes it all worthwhile. My gosh, I must have spent half my life for a

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:20.960
while there, running around and chasing earthworms to feed this little robin. But I just wanted you

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:27.440
to see that he was all right. He grew up, and I was so proud to let him go. This year, I raised

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.940
seven little birds, and they all went. We had a

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.720
everything from robins to starlings, even,

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.040
I even raised some starlings,

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.820
and I know they may not be the best bird in the world,

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:39.120
but I like them, I like all little birds.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:41.660
There we go.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.630
And the lady you saw there on the screen that was with me,

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.020
as I say, she's the bird lady here in Muncie,

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.600
and we're trying to put together a show to you

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.490
that will show what she does

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.070
and how she takes care of all these birds,

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.730
and maybe you'll get to see that in the future.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:58.290
Okay, I've put little trees all back here in the background.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:02.440
Now I just want to create a little mist at the base.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.590
So I'm just going to tap, give it a little rub,

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.760
tap, and go like so.

