See there?

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.650
It makes it nice and misty and soft.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.950
Now then, let me wash that round brush.

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:21.930
Wash it the same way.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.570
There's a screen in the bottom of this bucket

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.960
that I scrubbed the brush against.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.980
Shake it off, and it's almost as much.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:30.950
One is a big brush.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.760
Now then, let's have some snow on top of all these.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.320
So I'm going right into the titanium white.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.260
Tap. Tap firmly.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.660
Use the top of these bristles.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.060
That's where you really want to do the tapping.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.170
Go right up in here and get some paint on them, okay?

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.170
Let's go right up in here.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.870
Now, use just the top bristles

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:57.540
and begin laying all kinds of little snow-covered areas

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:58.440
on these trees.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:06.310
see there you can just put thousands and thousands of leaves just with a couple of strokes but layer

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:11.640
these see that once again creates distance i know you get tired of hearing me say about distance

